==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|Grand Poobah}}

===Etymology===
From Pooh-Bah, the name of the character in [[w:Gilbert and Sullivan|Gilbert and Sullivan]]'s ''[[w:The Mikado|The Mikado]]'' (1885).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ɡɹænd ˈpuːbɑː/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|head=[[grand]] [[poobah]]}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic|colloquial|often|humorous}} A [[person]] who is [[important]] or [[high-ranking]].
#: ''He once played golf with the '''grand poobah''' of their company.''
# An extremely pompous person.

